                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 1,
                  "column": 12,
                  "offset": 11
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Quantum Computing relies heavily on principles of Quantum Mechanics such as Quantum Superposition and Quantum Entanglement. CNOT Gate (or sometimes also known as CX Gate) is can be used for entangling the state of 2 Qubits, which makes it a very important Quantum Gate. In this chapter of the OpenQASM Tutorial, you will be learning about how to apply CNOT Gate on Qubits.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 3,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 13
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 3,
                      "column": 373,
                      "offset": 385
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 3,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 13
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 3,
                  "column": 373,
                  "offset": 385
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "CNOT(or CX) is a fundamental two-Qubit gate in the field of Quantum Computing. In OpenQASM, CNOT is a built-in gate and therefore OpenQASM provides the syntax to apply a CNOT Gate on two Qubits.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 5,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 387
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 5,
                      "column": 195,
                      "offset": 581
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 5,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 387
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 5,
                  "column": 195,
                  "offset": 581
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "depth": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "CNOT Gate",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 7,
                      "column": 4,
                      "offset": 586
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 7,
                      "column": 13,
                      "offset": 595
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 7,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 583
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 7,
                  "column": 13,
                  "offset": 595
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "The CNOT Gate is a two-Qubit gate which applies a conditional NOT Gate on a target Qubit if and only if the control Qubit is in state |1>",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 597
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 138,
                      "offset": 734
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 9,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 597
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 9,
                  "column": 138,
                  "offset": 734
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "The following syntax is used for applying the CNOT Gate with control Qubit qr1[index] and target Qubit qr2[index]–",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 11,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 736
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 11,
                      "column": 117,
                      "offset": 852
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 11,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 736
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 11,
                  "column": 117,
                  "offset": 852
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "qasm",
              "meta": null,
              "value": "cx qr1[index], qr2[index];",
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 13,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 854
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 15,
                  "column": 4,
                  "offset": 892
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "strong",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "value": "Note:",
                      "position": {
                        "start": {
                          "line": 17,
                          "column": 3,
                          "offset": 896
                        },
                        "end": {
                          "line": 17,
                          "column": 8,
                          "offset": 901
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 17,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 894
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 17,
                      "column": 10,
                      "offset": 903
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": " CNOT is a built-in gate therefore cx is a reserved keyword.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 17,
                      "column": 10,
                      "offset": 903
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 17,
                      "column": 70,
                      "offset": 963
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 17,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 894
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 17,
